Fattuh, Bell's guide, played by Jay Abdo.

9
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
T.E. Lawrence, played by Robert Pattinson.

10
01:00:57,142 --> 01:01:03,142
Florence Bell, played by Jenny Agutter.

11
01:07:02,857 --> 01:07:08,857
Queen of the Desert is a 2015 American epic biographical drama film written and directed by Werner Herzog and is based on the
life of British traveller, writer, archaeologist, explorer, cartographer and political officer Gertrude Bell.

12
01:13:08,571 --> 01:13:14,571
The film follows Bell's life chronologically, from
her early twenties until her death.

13
01:19:14,285 --> 01:19:20,285
It was Herzog's first feature film in six years after his
2009 film My Son, My Son, What Have Ye Done?

14
01:25:20,000 --> 01:25:26,000
The film stars Nicole Kidman, James Franco, Damian Lewis and Robert Pattinson.

15
01:31:25,714 --> 01:31:31,714
After going through many delays and casting problems, production finally took place
from December 2013 to March 2014 in Morocco, Jordan and England.

16
01:37:31,428 --> 01:37:37,428
It was screened in the main competition section of the 65th Berlin
International Film Festival and had its premiere on February 6, 2015.

17
01:43:37,142 --> 01:43:43,142
It had a theatrical release in Germany on September 3, 2015.

18
01:49:42,857 --> 01:49:48,857
The film received mostly negative reviews from critics and was also a major financial
disappointment, grossing $2 million against a $36 million production budget.

19
01:55:48,571 --> 01:55:54,571
The film explores themes of middle east, persia,
unrequited love, travel writer, adventurer.

20
02:01:54,285 --> 02:02:00,285
The tone is emotional.
